==============================================================================
PART 1: Danger-comb geometry of a parked runner w == 0 (mod 14)
==============================================================================
w=  14: meas(D_w)=1/7  (=0.142857)  teeth=14  tooth_width=1/98=0.0102041  spacing=1/14=0.0714286
w=  28: meas(D_w)=1/7  (=0.142857)  teeth=28  tooth_width=1/196=0.00510204  spacing=1/28=0.0357143
w=  84: meas(D_w)=1/7  (=0.142857)  teeth=84  tooth_width=1/588=0.00170068  spacing=1/84=0.0119048
w=  98: meas(D_w)=1/7  (=0.142857)  teeth=98  tooth_width=1/686=0.00145773  spacing=1/98=0.0102041
w= 168: meas(D_w)=1/7  (=0.142857)  teeth=168  tooth_width=1/1176=0.00085034  spacing=1/168=0.00595238
CHECK: meas(D_w) = 1/7 exactly for all w (each tooth width 1/(7w), w teeth).

So the comb D_w has w teeth at centers k/w (k=0..w-1), each of HALF-width
  (1/14)/w = 1/(14w). The GAP between consecutive teeth (safe between teeth)
  has length  1/w - 2/(14w) = 1/w - 1/(7w) = (6/7)/w = 6/(7w).
  As w -> infinity, the comb becomes arbitrarily FINE: the largest safe
  interval BETWEEN teeth has length 6/(7w) -> 0.  <-- 'thin comb' intuition.

